  <title>Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00564</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f041fc0a-7ba0-4b0c-8e18-116bfd8096f7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will write, solve, and graph linear inequalities in two variables.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Determine which side of the line the solutions to the inequality will fall, given a
          two-variable inequality and the graph of the related equation.</item>
        <item>Describe the graph that represents the solutions to a linear inequality in two
          variables.</item>
      </list>


      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>2.11.1: Using Computation and Reasoning</item>
        <item>2.11.2: Finding Solutions to Inequalities on the Coordinate Plane<list id="list-00003">
            <item>2.11.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>2.11.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>2.11.3: Sketching Solutions to Inequalities<list id="list-00004">
            <item>2.11.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>2.11.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>2.11.4: Shading Boundary Line Regions</item>
      </list>

      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis effect="bold">practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>2.10.7: Practice</item>
        <item>2.10.8: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>

    </section>
  </content>
</document>